<h3 id=3D"complexity-analysis">Complexity Analysis</h3>
<p><strong>Time complexity:</strong> The time complexity of <code>find_all_=
subsets</code> is <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math =
xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo=
 stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=E2=8B=85</m=
o><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=3D"app=
lication/x-tex">O(n^2\cdot n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span c=
lass=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"><span class=
=3D"strut" style=3D"height: 1.0641em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><spa=
n class=3D"mord mathnormal" style=3D"margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><spa=
n class=3D"mopen">(</span><span class=3D"mord"><span class=3D"mord mathnorm=
al">n</span><span class=3D"msupsub"><span class=3D"vlist-t"><span class=3D"=
vlist-r"><span class=3D"vlist" style=3D"height: 0.8141em;"><span style=3D"t=
op: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class=3D"pstrut" style=3D"height=
: 2.7em;"></span><span class=3D"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span clas=
s=3D"mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>=
<span class=3D"mspace" style=3D"margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class=
=3D"mbin">=E2=8B=85</span><span class=3D"mspace" style=3D"margin-right: 0.2=
222em;"></span></span><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"h=
eight: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal=
">n</span><span class=3D"mclose">)</span></span></span></span>. This is bec=
ause the state space tree has a depth of <span class=3D"katex"><span class=
=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><seman=
tics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">n</a=
nnotation></semantics></math></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=
=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height: 0.430=
6em;"></span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span></span> =
and a branching factor of 2 since there are two decisions we make at each s=
tate. For each of the <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><m=
ath xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn=
><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">2n</annotation=
></semantics></math></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true">=
<span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height: 0.6444em;"></sp=
an><span class=3D"mord">2</span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span></s=
pan></span></span> subsets created, we make a copy of them and add the copy=
 to the output, which takes <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-math=
ml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi=
>O</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo>=
</mrow><annotation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semant=
ics></math></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span cla=
ss=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.=
25em;"></span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal" style=3D"margin-right: 0.0277=
8em;">O</span><span class=3D"mopen">(</span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal"=
>n</span><span class=3D"mclose">)</span></span></span></span> time. This re=
sults in a total time complexity of <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"ka=
tex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><=
mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msu=
p><mo>=E2=8B=85</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo></mrow><annotati=
on encoding=3D"application/x-tex">O(n^2\cdot n)</annotation></semantics></m=
ath></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"b=
ase"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height: 1.0641em; vertical-align: -0.25=
em;"></span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal" style=3D"margin-right: 0.02778e=
m;">O</span><span class=3D"mopen">(</span><span class=3D"mord"><span class=
=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span><span class=3D"msupsub"><span class=3D"vlist-t=
"><span class=3D"vlist-r"><span class=3D"vlist" style=3D"height: 0.8141em;"=
><span style=3D"top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class=3D"pstrut=
" style=3D"height: 2.7em;"></span><span class=3D"sizing reset-size6 size3 m=
tight"><span class=3D"mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></sp=
an></span></span><span class=3D"mspace" style=3D"margin-right: 0.2222em;"><=
/span><span class=3D"mbin">=E2=8B=85</span><span class=3D"mspace" style=3D"=
margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"=
strut" style=3D"height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class=
=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span><span class=3D"mclose">)</span></span></span><=
/span>.</p>
<p><strong>Space complexity:</strong> The space complexity is <span class=
=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/19=
98/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mi=
>n</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=3D"applicat=
ion/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=3D"katex-=
html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=
=3D"height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class=3D"mord mathn=
ormal" style=3D"margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class=3D"mopen">(</=
span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span><span class=3D"mclose">)</span=
></span></span></span> because the maximum depth of the recursion tree is <=
span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www=
.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation enc=
oding=3D"application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span c=
lass=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"><span class=
=3D"strut" style=3D"height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class=3D"mord mathnorma=
l">n</span></span></span></span>. The algorithm also maintains the <code>cu=
rr_subset</code> data structure, which also contributes <span class=3D"kate=
x"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/=
MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><=
mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=3D"application/x-te=
x">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=3D"katex-html" ar=
ia-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"heig=
ht: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal" s=
tyle=3D"margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class=3D"mopen">(</span><sp=
an class=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span><span class=3D"mclose">)</span></span>=
</span></span> space. Note, the <code>res</code> array does not contribute =
to space complexity.</p><div class=3D"style_markCompleteWrap__YEi4w"><butto=
